// In Thaana every consonant letter carries one mark: a vowel sign (fili)
// or the sukun (no vowel). So the rule for a consonant letter gives only
// the consonant, and the rule for the mark after it gives the vowel.
// The special cases (some letters with sukun, a bare noonu, ai and au,
// and alifu at the start of a word) are commented where they appear.
//
// letter groups (set in tr_languages.c):
// A - vowel signs (fili): U+07A6 to U+07AF
// B - vowel signs and sukun: U+07A6 to U+07B0
// C - consonants: U+0780 to U+07A5, U+07B1


